ng with a successor draft merging with no verdict artifact of any kind under both never and when-minting, while a spine draft still owes its round. THE DIAL AT THE SCHEDULER, the half a reader could otherwise only take on trust: a committing ADJUDICATE session is driven through the loop's own bookkeeping arm on a closed-lane repository at every dial value - including the `always` no repository fixture had reached - and the review queue it leaves is asserted together with the train-scoped diff range and the recorded judging family, which is what \"exactly as a committing BUILD does\" has to mean. Its INPUT is driven beside it: a branch carrying its spec in BOTH homes, the terminal copy drafting a spine successor and a stale active copy an ordinary one, is asserted to answer the scheduler and the merge gate the SAME way, with the shared precedence also driven pure on a two-path list and on the empty one. THE SHARED DEFINITION, in BOTH its dimensions. WHICH TREE: the C2 review-owed derivation answers owed after a rework and served after a fresh round, and record-only commits after the verdict re-owe nothing. HOW MANY PHASES: at a declared policy of 2 a lone logged REVIEW-A APPROVE is REFUSED by name and the gate clears only once a governing REVIEW-B joins it at the same identity; and the half-drawn round a killed run leaves - REVIEW-A served, the in-memory phase queue gone - is answered by both readers together, the derivation naming REVIEW-B and ONLY REVIEW-B while the gate refuses, then both agreeing once it lands, with the same fixture asserted SERVED at policy 1 so the answer is proven to come from the declared count. The phase span is driven pure at the values neither caller reaches - a negative policy, which a bare slice would answer by slicing from the END, and an over-dialled one - and an unparseable or refusable round is owed on both sides: it is drawn again and never clears the gate. The one class the readers still disagree on is a dissent: it is served for `